###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_7afbed84_7593_4a23_bd88_9d9c6b04e8f6
<https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_7afbed84_7593_4a23_bd88_9d9c6b04e8f6> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_55354438_7000_4284_b1b9_59d60c2261b9> ;
                                                                  rdfs:domain <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c5ddfdba_c074_4aa4_ad6b_1ac4942d300d> ;
                                                                  owl:propertyDisjointWith <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_9a50a0ae_841a_46fe_8b23_3df319b60611> ;
                                                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/mereocausality#> ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "hasTemporalPart"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A relation that identify a proper item part of the whole, whose parts always cover the full spatial extension of the whole within a time interval."@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f> """A temporal part of an item cannot both cause and be caused by any other proper part of the item.
A temporal part is not constraint to be causally self-connected, i.e. it can be either an item or a collection. We therefore introduce two subproperties in order to distinguish between both cases."""@en ,
                                                                                                                                    "In EMMO FOL this is a defined property. In OWL temporal relations are primitive."@en .


