                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A programming language entity expressing a formal detailed plan of what a software is intended to do."@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f> "A source code is the companion of an application, being it the entity used to generate the application list of CPU executable instructions."@en ,
                                                                                                                                    "Source code (also referred to as source or code) is the version of software as it is originally written (i.e., typed into a computer) by a human in plain text (i.e., human readable alphanumeric characters)."@en .

