                                                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/materials#> ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "CompositePhysicalObject"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13> "A composite physical object is made of bonded objects (i.e. characterised by their quantum states using a Schrodinger equation approach) that are connected together by elementary particles travelling between them. These elemenentary particles are real particles, describing the existance of a classical field (e.g. Coulomb potential between charged particles)."@en ;
