                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ῥόδος"^^xsd:anyURI ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "IRI"@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "An Internationalized Resource Identifier (IRI) is a compact sequence of characters that identifies an abstract or physical resource. It is similar to URI, but greatly extends the allowed character set from ASCII to the Universal Character Set (Unicode/ISO 10646).."@en ;
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f> "IRIs are commonly used as identifiers for ontological entities, although the extended unicode character set is rarely used."@en ;
