                                                                                                    ] ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "BatterySystemSpecification"@en ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used for systems where the specification boundary extends beyond the battery pack to include inverters, thermal management infrastructure, battery management systems, energy management systems, or grid-interface equipment. Properties include system-level power, energy, round-trip efficiency, and integration requirements."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A specification describing a complete energy storage system comprising one or more battery packs with integrated power electronics, control systems, and auxiliary components."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c> "The boundary between BatteryPackSpecification and BatterySystemSpecification is application-dependent. In IEC 62619 the system includes the pack and BMS; in grid storage applications it extends to power conversion and site infrastructure. The system boundary must be stated explicitly in the specification record."@en .


