###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/battery#battery_142a444e_2575_41dd_8d69_52e438fc66d3
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/battery#battery_142a444e_2575_41dd_8d69_52e438fc66d3> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/battery#battery_a4ba7f50_5fe0_43f4_9862_4dd57e87a44c> ,
                                                                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                                                                      owl:onProperty <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_f702bad4_fc77_41f0_a26d_79f6444fd4f3> ;
                                                                                                      owl:someValuesFrom <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/battery#battery_9acfeea6_ca7f_4b97_9844_c38edf6387ec>
                                                                                                    ] ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "BatteryModuleSpecification"@en ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used when the module is a distinct functional or commercial unit with its own certification, testing identity, or mechanical enclosure, separate from both individual cells and the complete pack. Properties typically include cell count, series-parallel configuration, module voltage and capacity, and module-level thermal management."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A specification describing the design and electrical configuration of a battery module comprising multiple cells arranged in a defined series-parallel topology."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c> "Module boundaries vary significantly across manufacturers and standards. Clarify whether the specification refers to a cell group (electrically connected cells without enclosure), a mechanically integrated module, or a sub-pack before applying this class. In cell-to-pack and cell-to-body architectures, the module level may be absent entirely."@en .


