###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/battery#battery_88b7849f_4c33_4206_a674_2489bf08d8b8
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/battery#battery_88b7849f_4c33_4206_a674_2489bf08d8b8> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                    rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_65a007dc_2550_46b0_b394_3346c67fbb69> ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A battery system may contain one or more battery packs. It is distinguished from a battery pack by the inclusion of power electronics and active control systems that condition and regulate energy flow between the battery and the application. In small or simple systems these components may be integrated into the pack enclosure; in large systems they are physically separate."@en ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "BatterySystem"@en ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used for systems where the functional boundary extends beyond the battery pack to include power conversion (inverters, DC-DC converters), active thermal management infrastructure, and application-level energy management. Characterised by system-level performance including rated power, rated energy, round-trip efficiency, and grid or vehicle interface specifications."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A complete energy storage assembly comprising one or more battery packs together with integrated power electronics, thermal management, and control systems, functioning as a single deployable unit."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c> "The boundary between BatteryPack and BatterySystem is defined differently across standards. The system boundary must be stated explicitly when reporting system-level properties."@en .


