                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "the chemistry-specific subclasses (LithiumIonIronPhosphateBattery and siblings) form a closed, curated set of industry-standard chemistries; additions are deliberate policy decisions, and stoichiometry variants (e.g. NMC811) are expressed at the material level rather than as new battery classes"@en ,
                                                                                                                               "the chemistry-specific subclasses are defined classes: assert the cell's electrode composition and a reasoner infers the chemistry classification; they should not be asserted directly"@en ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "LithiumIonBattery"@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_26bf1bef_d192_4da6_b0eb_d2209698fb54> "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2822895" ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_50c298c2_55a2_4068_b3ac_4e948c33181f> "https://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&ievref=482-05-07" ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25> "https://dbpedia.org/page/Lithium-ion_battery"@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "secondary battery with an organic solvent electrolyte and positive and negative electrodes which utilize an intercalation compound in which lithium is stored"@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithium-ion_battery"@en .


