                                                                                                    ] ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "BatteryPackSpecification"@en ;
                                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The battery pack is the primary commercially traded unit in most applications and carries regulatory compliance, warranty, and end-of-life obligations. Properties typically include pack voltage and energy, cell or module configuration, battery management system type, thermal management design, housing class, and application-specific performance parameters."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_5f7abc2a_5b50_41c3_8def_c8ba7c3b083e> "Pack specifications aggregate and extend cell or module specifications. Where cell-level data is available, link the pack specification to its constituent BatteryCellSpecification instances to enable traceability from pack performance to cell-level material data."@en ;
                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A specification describing the design, configuration, and performance characteristics of a complete battery pack intended for delivery as a traded unit to an application system."@en .


