                                                                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "GasAdsorptionPorosimetry"@en ;
                                                                                            <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "Gas Adsorption Porosimetry is a method used for analyzing the surface area and porosity of materials. In this method, a gas, typically nitrogen or argon, is adsorbed onto the surface of the material at various pressures and temperatures."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/characterisation-methodology/chameo#Grinding
