###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/chemical-substance#substance_9f3b59a2_b2af_4b5b_919c_0c68d10f3edf
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/chemical-substance#substance_9f3b59a2_b2af_4b5b_919c_0c68d10f3edf> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/chemical-substance#substance_b325bdd7_0adf_4522_a4ef_20cd6929e094> ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Perfluorocarboxylic acids (PFCAs) are a distinct and widely recognized subclass of PFAS with a shared structural motif and consistent chemical behavior. They are frequently referenced in environmental science, toxicology, and regulatory frameworks as a separate category from other fluorinated substances. Including this term enables precise semantic classification and interoperability across chemical substance ontologies."@en ,
                                                                                                                                            "Perfluorocarboxylic acids include compounds such as trifluoroacetic acid and perfluorooctanoic acid, which are relevant due to their persistence, bioaccumulation potential, and industrial use. The class is commonly treated"@en ;
                                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "PerfluorocarboxylicAcid"@en ;
                                                                                                 <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A perfluoroalkyl substance consisting of a fully fluorinated carbon chain terminating in a carboxylic acid functional group."@en .


