###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_743c71a3_b80c_42e3_92fa_13a67b8167df
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_743c71a3_b80c_42e3_92fa_13a67b8167df> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_02eb0465_4f94_453c_8c1f_5ddf80134634> ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Commonly measured at 25 °C, 35 °C, and 45 °C with cells held at 50% or 100% state of charge; Arrhenius or power-law models are used to extrapolate to operational lifetime."@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "CalendarLife"@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Characterises time-dependent degradation that occurs independently of cycling load. Particularly relevant for automotive (typically 15-year targets) and stationary storage (20+ year targets) applications."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4c8480cf_56de_41da_8699_f12a9033313a> "CalendarLife and CycleLife are independent quantities. A cell may reach calendar end-of-life before its rated cycle count if stored at elevated temperature or high state of charge for extended periods."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_5f7abc2a_5b50_41c3_8def_c8ba7c3b083e> "End-of-life is typically defined as 80% capacity retention or 20% power fade relative to initial values; the criterion used must be stated alongside the value."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "The time elapsed from initial commissioning until an electrochemical cell or battery reaches a defined end-of-life criterion under specified storage or use conditions, independent of the number of charge–discharge cycles performed."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c> "Strongly dependent on storage temperature and state of charge. Values reported without these conditions specified cannot be meaningfully compared. Accelerated ageing tests at elevated temperature require validated time–temperature superposition models to extrapolate to use conditions."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_74459386_875c_4303_b774_60125b599d06
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_74459386_875c_4303_b774_60125b599d06> rdf:type owl:Class ;
