###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_8abde9d0_84f6_4b4f_a87e_86028a397100
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_8abde9d0_84f6_4b4f_a87e_86028a397100> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_9b3b4668_0795_4a35_9965_2af383497a26> ;
                                                                                                      rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_a7a4614f_2426_46f3_8475_cda4a9fabfce> ,
                                                                                                                   <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_b7781ebc_90a7_4f19_997f_aed28dee1b01> ,
                                                                                                                   <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_d3c0078e_c1d3_461e_873d_e5c3adf441c5> ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "NominalCapacity"@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The value for 'nominal capacity' is provided by manufacturers as an indication of the expected performance of the device under a set of defined nominal conditions. It serves as a benchmark for comparing different devices."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_5f7abc2a_5b50_41c3_8def_c8ba7c3b083e> "To ensure meaningful comparisons, nominal capacity values should always be evaluated under matching test conditions."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "the rated capacity that is representative of the typical value associated with a cell as stated by the manufacturer"@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c> "While nominal capacity provides a useful reference, actual capacity depends on various factors, including temperature, rate, and state-of-health."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_cc65321f_1964_4f16_aea3_2a8edf2f3394> <https://w3id.org/emmo#AmpereHour> ,
                                                                                                                                                                        <https://w3id.org/emmo#MilliAmpereHour> .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_8ae1ee53_5866_4d94_8715_35e90626fa55
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_8ae1ee53_5866_4d94_8715_35e90626fa55> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_0f007072_a8dd_4798_b865_1bf9363be627> ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An ImmersionElectrode is a common electrochemical configuration where the electrode operates fully submerged in a liquid electrolyte, distinct from the existing terms GasDiffusionElectrode and AirElectrode. Addition of this term improves clarity when modelling electrode–electrolyte interfaces and complements existing electrode classifications."@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ImmersionElectrode"@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "This concept contrasts with gas-diffusion and partially wetted electrodes by explicitly requiring full immersion in a liquid phase, which impacts transport phenomena, reaction kinetics, and modelling assumptions.e"@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "an electrode designed to operate fully immersed in a liquid electrolyte"@en .


