###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_964cd426_f3cf_4a52_8c5d_0490cf48edb5
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_964cd426_f3cf_4a52_8c5d_0490cf48edb5> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_9bf40017_3f58_4030_ada7_cb37a3dfda2d> ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ACIR"@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Determined by electrochemical impedance spectroscopy or by a single-frequency AC perturbation technique. Typically reported in milliohms (mΩ)."@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ACInternalResistance"@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "At 1 kHz, reactive contributions from double-layer capacitance and Warburg diffusion are suppressed for typical battery geometries, making the result a practical approximation of ohmic resistance."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4c8480cf_56de_41da_8699_f12a9033313a> "The measurement frequency must be stated alongside the value. At frequencies above a few kilohertz, inductive reactance from cell tabs and interconnects can dominate the measured impedance."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "The magnitude of the complex impedance of an electrochemical cell at a specified alternating-current frequency, typically 1 kHz."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c> "Characteristically lower than DCInternalResistance because electrochemical kinetic contributions are excluded at the measurement frequency. The two quantities must not be used interchangeably."@en .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_97bc06e6_6141_47ec_9e81_fd9e6a5b07c7
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_97bc06e6_6141_47ec_9e81_fd9e6a5b07c7> rdf:type owl:Class ;
