                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Manufacturers define the value for 'maximum capacity' as the upper performance limit that a device in a batch will typically achieve. The maximum capacity is larger than the nominal capacity, and acts as an indicator of the spread in performacne in a given batch of devices."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "the maximum amount of electric charge that can be reversible stored within an electrochemical device"@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c> "For real applications, the maximum capacity is affected by environmental conditions, rate of operation, and state-of-heath and can deviate from the reported value."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_cc65321f_1964_4f16_aea3_2a8edf2f3394> <https://w3id.org/emmo#AmpereHour> ,
                                                                                                                                                                        <https://w3id.org/emmo#MilliAmpereHour> .


###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_b79d4f9e_5727_4895_8d7f_5fc18d83eb90
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_b79d4f9e_5727_4895_8d7f_5fc18d83eb90> rdf:type owl:Class ;
