                                                                                                      rdfs:comment "In lithium-ion degradation-mode analysis this is the loss of lithium inventory (LLI). It is a ratio of capacities, not a mass, volume or amount fraction; a cell can lose cyclable inventory while its electrodes keep their full capacity."@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ChargeCarrierInventoryLossFraction"@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_0a0de817_addc_46a5_8ba2_255d48cdf366> ,
                                                                                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_652b94f1_290d_4d9e_820a_eda4c71eb90d> ,
                                                                                                                                                    <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_b1b406fe_2579_4f13_b1ac_84fc3fd0e15f> ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "fraction of the charge-carrier inventory of a cell lost to degradation, the inventory being expressed as the capacity it could deliver: the difference between a reference and the present inventory capacity, divided by the reference"@en .


