                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_0fa6566e_500f_4d24_baa9_b2b22c9a0b72> "The term \"anode\" is often used interchangably with \"negative electrode\" even though it only applies while the cell is being discharged. When the cell is being charged the negatve electrode becomes the cathode."@en ;
