###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_f42746ba_724c_4ab9_aa04_61b062f23076
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_f42746ba_724c_4ab9_aa04_61b062f23076> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                                      rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_f76884f7_964e_488e_9bb7_1b2453e9e817> ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Electrochemical (flow) cells require gaskets to seal the electrolyte compartments and define the active electrode area through compression. Gaskets are a distinct, functionally critical cell component that determines compression ratio, contact resistance, and electrolyte leakage."@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Gasket"@en ;
                                                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Gaskets in electrochemical (flow) cells are typically made from polymer materials (e.g. PTFE, Viton, silicone) and their thickness directly determines electrode compression, which affects mass transport and contact resistance. They are a required component in any flow cell metadata description alongside electrodes, membrane, and flow field. The term is distinct from Separator and Membrane which describe ionically active components, whereas a gasket is purely a mechanical sealing element."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9> "A deformable sealing component placed between cell assembly layers to prevent fluid leakage and define the active electrode area through controlled compression."@en ;
                                                                                                      <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d> "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gasket" .


